### SECTION 4: ARCHITECTURE HIGHLIGHTS

#### 4.1 Cryptographic Foundation
- **Signature Algorithm:** Ed25519 (NIST P-256 equivalent security)
- **Hash Function:** SHA-256 (NIST-approved)
- **KDF (Future v5.1):** Argon2id + AES-256-GCM
- **Key Storage:** Encrypted at rest (v5.1), plaintext bootstrap (v5.0.0)
- **Verification:** NFC-normalized canonical bytes, BTreeMap sorting

#### 4.2 Concurrency Model
- **Registry:** Arc<Mutex<AgentRegistry>> — thread-safe mutable state
- **Store:** Arc<RwLock<AdnStore>> — concurrent read-heavy access
- **Governance:** Arc<Mutex<GovernanceModule>> — exclusive voting state
- **Design:** Tokio async/await, handle 100+ concurrent agents (v5.0.0), 10k+ planned (v5.2)

#### 4.3 Data Durability
- **Append-only audit log:** SQLite, all messages immutable
- **Hash-chain:** Each message references parent SHA-256
- **Recovery:** Full replay capability from genesis
- **Future (v5.1):** Checkpoint/pruning at 1M message boundary

#### 4.4 Byzantine Resilience
- **Consensus:** 2/3 quorum voting (alice, bob, charlie)
- **Failure tolerance:** 1 faulty agent = consensus unaffected
- **Decision binding:** Stored in audit trail, immutable
- **Governance:** Restricted council enforces policy voting
- **Future (v5.2):** Leader election fallback, formal proof (Coq/Isabelle)

