### SECTION 7: v5.1 ROADMAP (Q4 2026, 331 Hours)

#### 7.1 Critical Path (Parallelizable)
```
Timeline: 6-8 weeks (parallel work)

PHASE 1 (Weeks 1-2):
  ✓ Layer 6: TLS 1.3 mutual authentication (100h)
  ✓ Layer 8: AES-256-GCM message encryption (50h)

PHASE 2 (Weeks 2-3):
  ✓ Rate limiting + proof-of-work (25h)
  ✓ Encrypted key storage (20h)

PHASE 3 (Weeks 4-6):
  ✓ Database checkpointing + pruning (75h)
  ✓ Testing suite (40h)

PHASE 4 (Weeks 6-8):
  ✓ Documentation updates (20h)
  ✓ Release preparation (checklist)
```

#### 7.2 Layer Features (v5.1 New)

**Layer 6: TLS 1.3 Mutual Authentication**
- Server cert + private key at `~/.cstl/server_*.pem`
- Agent certs at `~/.cstl/agent_{name}_{cert,key}.pem`
- Mutual auth verified: all agents require valid cert
- Backward compatibility: unsigned payloads still accepted
- Risk: Medium (async complexity), Effort: 80-120h

**Layer 8: AES-256-GCM Encryption**
- Encryption key derived from TLS session key
- Nonce: timestamp (Unix ms) + random 64-bit suffix
- Defense-in-depth: orthogonal to TLS
- Signature verification post-decryption
- Risk: Low (audited crypto), Effort: 40-60h

**Additional Features:**
- Rate limiting: Per-IP (1000/min), per-agent (500/min), per-purpose (custom)
- Proof-of-Work: SHA-256 leading 24-bit zeros, ~16M attempts expected
- Key encryption: Argon2 KDF, password-protected storage
- DB checkpointing: Snapshots every 100k messages, archive old entries

